","ctaButton":"Go to homepage"},"Tsx30":{"title":"TMX Money | TSX Today | Canadian Stock Exchange","metaDescr":"Get free real-time stock prices for the TSX today or use our premium investor tools to research your next investment on TSX, TSXV, or Alpha.","metaKeywords":"TMX Money, TSX, investment ideas, free real-time stock prices, TSX Venture","metaDesc2021":"TSX30™ is a ranking of the top 30 performers on Toronto Stock Exchange based on 3-year share price appreciation.","metaDesc2022":"This year`s TSX30 winners have demonstrated their willingness to innovate their core offering, transform how they operate and diversify their business for resilience and growth.","metaDesc2023":"This year`s TSX30 winners have demonstrated their willingness to innovate their core offering, transform how they operate and diversify their business for resilience and growth.","Navbar":{"overview":"OVERVIEW","tsxList":"2025 TSX30 LIST","ranking":"Ranking","perspectives":"PERSPECTIVES FROM BUSINESS LEADERS","inMedia":"In the Media","methodology":"Methodology","download":"Download","about":"About","keyStats":"Key Stats"},"Banner":{"text":"EXELLENCE IN GROWTH"},"Rising":{"title":"INNOVATE. TRANSFORM. DIVERSIFY.","subTitle":"Top 30 companies in Canada ","content1":"While TSX listed companies posted solid returns during the pandemic, there’s no denying it has been a difficult year for investors and issuers. The companies featured on this year’s TSX30 list showed they could ","content2":" and stand out from the crowd. Over the past three years, they have proven their ability to ","content3":" despite unprecedented challenges. In post-COVID normal, they demonstrate their resilience and the drive to continue to ","content4":" as they navigate the changing shape of business and the economy.","desc":"Navigating the path forward and creating positive returns for investors requires a bold new approach. This year`s TSX30™ winners, a ranking of the top 30 performers on Toronto Stock Exchange, have demonstrated their willingness to innovate their core offering, transform how they operate, and diversify their business for resilience and growth.","compete":"compete","grow":"grow","excel":"excel","downloadList":"Download List","sharePrice":"Average 3-year adjusted price performance","marketCapital":"3-year market capitalization increase","companyComposite":"Companies in the S\u0026P/TSX Composite Index","graduates":"of TSX30 companies are graduates from TSX Venture Exchange","sharePrice2":"Average 3-year share price performance","marketCapital2":"3-year market capitalization increase","CompositeIndex":"of TSX30 companies are in the S\u0026P/TSX Composite Index","download":"Download Infographic"},"Winners":{"tsxWinners":"TSX30 {year} Winners","ticker":"Ticker","company":"Company","location":"Location","sharePrice":"3-YR Share Price","uniquePerspectives":"Unique Perspectives from Canadian Business Leaders","learnMore":"Learn More","seeMore":"See More","videos":"Articles","articles":"{count} Articles","thought":"Thought Leadership","perf":"3-Year Performance","downloadList":"Download List"},"Media":{"text":"TSX30 in the media","description":"Last updated: Apr 30, 2020, 9:00 AM ET, source: Quotemedia","headlines":"In the headlines","readArticle":"Read article","seeAllNews":"See All News"},"Ranking":{"text":"Ranking Methodology","content1":"The following criteria were applied to TSX corporate issuers","content2":"Corporate operating business listed on TSX on June 30, 2020","content3":"Listed on TSX for a minimum of 3 years or, if a TSXV graduate, a combination of TSX and TSXV for a minimum of 3 years with at least 1 year on TSX","content4":"Closing dividend-adjusted share price of at least $0.50 on June 30, 2017","content5":"Minimum market cap of $75 million on June 30, 2017","content6":"This left 546 companies that qualified for the 2020 TSX30 ranking.","content7":"These companies were ranked based on 3-year dividend-adjusted share price performance.","content8":"Historical share prices have been adjusted for dividends and/or stock consolidations. TSX considered companies’ compliance with Exchange Requirements and exercised discretion when determining qualified candidates.","content9":"All data current as of June 30, 2020. All currencies reported in Canadian dollars.","content10":"Source: TSX/TSXV Market Intelligence Group. Share prices and historical dividend-adjusted share prices from S\u0026P Capital IQ.","content11":"* TSX30 is a ranking of the top 30 performers on Toronto Stock Exchange over a three-year period based on dividend-adjusted share price appreciation.","listHeading":"Corporate operating business listed on TSX that qualified for the 2025 TSX30 ranking. These companies met the following criteria:","list1":"Corporate operating business listed on TSX on June 30, 2025.","list2":"Listed on TSX for a minimum of 3 years or if a TSX Venture Exchange graduate, a combination of TSX and TSXV for a minimum of 3 years with at least 1 year on TSX.","list3":"Closing share price of at least $0.50 on June 30, 2022.","list4":"Closing share price of at least $0.50 on June 30, 2022.","list5":"Minimum market cap of $75 million on June 30, 2022.","p1":"This left 517 companies that qualified for the 2025 TSX30 ranking. These companies were ranked based on a 3-year dividend-adjusted share price performance.","p3":"Historical share prices have been adjusted for dividends and/or stock consolidations. TSX considered companies' compliance with Exchange requirements and exercised discretion when determining qualified candidates. All data current as of June 30, 2025. All currencies reported in Canadian dollars.","p4":"All data current as of June 30, 2023. All currencies reported in Canadian dollars.","p5":"Source: TSX/TSXV Market Intelligence Group. Historical dividend-adjusted share prices from S\u0026P Capital IQ. ","i1":"Historical share prices have been adjusted for dividends and/or stock consolidations.","i2":"TSX considered companies' compliance with Exchange requirements and exercised discretion when determining qualified candidates.","i3":"All data current as of June 30, 2025. All currencies reported in Canadian dollars.","source":"Source: TSX/TSXV Market Intelligence Group. Historical dividend-adjusted share prices from S\u0026P Capital IQ."},"tagline":"EXCELLENCE IN GROWTH","videos":{"title":"Videos"},"aboutProgram":"About the Program","aboutProgramExpaination":"TSX30 is the flagship program recognizing the 30 top-performing companies on Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX). Eligible listed issuers are ranked based on their dividend-adjusted share price performance over a three-year period.","keyStats":"Key Stats","stats":{"first":"Average 3-Year Share Price Appreciation","firstValue":"431%","second":"3-Year Market Capitalization Growth","secondValue":"349%","third":"Companies Graduated from TSX Venture Exchange","thirdValue":"14","fourth":"in Market Cap Creation on TSX Over 3 Years","fourthValue":"$358B+"},"inTheMediaAndContent":"In the Media \u0026 Related Content","rankingMethodology":"Ranking Methodology","tsx30Ranking2023":"TSX30 2023 Ranking","tsx30Ranking2024":"2024 TSX30 Ranking","tsx30Ranking2025":"2025 TSX30® Ranking","hqLocation":"HQ Location","sharePrice":"3-Year Share Price Performance","globalOperations":"Global Operations","sustainabilityReport":"View Sustainability Report","companyWebsite":"View Company Website","viewMore":"View More","mediaPartners":"Partners","spp":"TSX30 is an annual ranking of the 30 top-performing companies on Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX). Eligible listed issuers are ranked based on their **dividend-adjusted share price performance over a three-year period.**","threeYearSPP":"3-Year Share Price Performance","sector":"Sector","hq":"HQ","website":"Website"},"AdminInfo":{"header":{"logoAlt":"TMX Money","title":"It’s your Quote Page, tell your story.","description":"Claim your Quote Page on TMX Money and upload an Investor Kit. Tell your story by sharing your content with over 1.5 million monthly visitors.","getStarted":"Get Started","statNumber1":"3.5M","statNumber2":"35M","statNumber3":"18M","statDescription1":"visits per month","statDescription2":"page views per month","statDescription3":"searches per month"},"section1":{"adminPortalImage":"Admin Portal Image","investorKitImage":"Investor Kit Image","title":"Create an Investor Kit for your Quote Page.","description":"Share your investor decks, fact sheets, ESG reports, videos, or articles with the TMX Money investor community."},"section2":{"accountManagementImage":"Account Management Image","title":"Increase the Visibility of Your Company.","description":"Upload content to your Investor Kit, and make it easy for relevant investors to find your company through search. "},"linxInfo":{"title":"Changes are Coming:","infoPageMsg":"In May, we will be streamlining the way you claim your Quote Page and upload Investor Kits to TMX Money. Stay tuned for updates.","dashboardMsg":"In May, we will be streamlining the way you claim your Quote Page on TMX Money. Stay tuned for updates.","mediaPageMsg":"In May, we will be streamlining the way you add / remove content on TMX Money. Stay tuned for updates.","infoParagraphs":{"here":"here","p1":"TSX and TSXV-listed companies can upload investor documents and videos to their TMX Money page via {link}, our issuer portal.","p2":"All companies that have TMX LINX accounts have a designated Principal Contact (an Officer or Director at the company who has the authority to bind the company and grant TMX LINX access to other users). The Principal Contact can give someone rights to upload investor documents and videos to a company's TMX Money page.","p3":"If you already have rights to upload investor documents and videos to TMX Money via your TMX LINX account, please click {link} to sign-in to TMX LINX.","p4":"If you would like to receive rights to upload investor documents and videos to TMX Money, please ask your company's Principal Contact to provide you with access.","p5":"If you do not know who your company's Principal Contact is, please email {link} so that we can approach them on your behalf and/or assist with onboarding your company to TMX LINX.","p6":"For any other questions about TMX Money, please visit our {link}"}}},"AddToWatchlistButton":{"addToWatchlistButton":"Add to Watchlist","subscribeToAlerts":"Subscribe to Alerts","createNewWatchlist":"Create a New Watchlist","getUnlimitedWatchLists":"Get Unlimited Watchlists","watchListName":"Watchlist Name","cancel":"Cancel","watchlistNameNotEmpty":"Watchlist name cannot be empty.","tryAgain":"Try Again","createWatchlist":"Create Watchlist","loading":"Loading","failedCreateWatchlistHeading":"Failed to create a new watchlist","failedCreateWatchlist":"Failed to create a new watchlist, please try again.","addedTo":"added to","addedToWl":"Added to watchlist","removedFrom":"removed from","successfullyCreatedWatchlist":"Successfully created a new watchlist","watchlistCreated":"has been created.","addedToWatchlist":"has been added to your new watchlist.","goToWatchlist":"Go to Watchlist","dismiss":"Dismiss","getUnlimitedSymbols":"Get Unlimited Symbols","reachedMaxSymbols":"You have reached the maximum of symbols you could add to this watchlist."}},"__APOLLO_STATE__":{},"stockList":{"stockListId":"RECENT_LISTINGS_SYMBOLS","name":"Recent Listings You May Have Missed in July","description":"Companies that recently commenced trading on TSX \u0026 TSXV.","longDescription":"Companies that recently commenced trading on TSX \u0026 TSXV.","metricTitle":"Market","listItems":[{"symbol":"ZCDX.U","longName":"BMO Credit Stress Opportunities ETF","rank":1,"metric":null,"price":30,"priceChange":0.04,"percentChange":0.133511,"volume":1,"__typename":"StockListItem"},{"symbol":"ALCH","longName":"Alchemy Labs Inc.","rank":2,"metric":null,"price":0.98,"priceChange":0,"percentChange":0,"volume":77401,"__typename":"StockListItem"},{"symbol":"AMAP","longName":"Amapá Minerals Holdings Inc.","ran